questions.text:
Study the code below:

```php
function generateFibonacci($n) {
   $num_1 = 0;
   $num_2 = 1;

      if($n == 1)
          echo $num_1;
      else if($n == 2)
          echo $num_2;
      for ($i = 3; $i <= $n; $i++) {
          $num_3 = $num_1 + $num_2;
          $num_1 = $num_2;
          $num_2 = $num_3;
      }

      echo $num_3;
}
```

a) Explain what the above function does. (2 marks)
b) What is the output generated when this function is executed with a value of 0
   assigned to $n (passed as the argument)? (1 mark)
c) Give a value when assigned to $n (passed as the argument) that will result in 8
   being displayed when this function executes. (1 mark)
d) How many times would the for loop execute in the function for a value of 5
   assigned to $n (passed as the argument)? (2 marks)
e) Let's assume that the function is called using argument value of 5. What are the
   values of $num_3, $num_1 and $num_2 at the end of the second iteration of the
   for loop? (3 marks)
f) Modify the function to make use of the conditional operator to replace the if else
   statement and to reduce the number of echo statements from three to one. (6
   marks)

questions.correctAnswer:
(a) Generates a value from the Fibonacci sequence by adding the preceding two values.
(b) With n=0 the loop never runs: $num_3 is undefined and a warning is possible; no numeric Fibonacci value is printed.
(c) n=7 gives 8.
(d) 3 iterations for n=5 (i=3,4,5).
(e) At the end of iteration 2: $num_3=2, $num_1=1, $num_2=2.
(f) Example:
function generateFibonacci($n) {
  $a=0; $b=1; $next=0;
  for ($i=3; $i<=$n; $i++) { $next=$a+$b; $a=$b; $b=$next; }
  echo $n===1 ? 0 : ($n===2 ? 1 : $next);
}

