questions.text:
Given below is a function that displays a specified number of numbers starting from 0
in the Fibonacci series.
function generateFibonacci($count){
  $num_1 = 0;
  $num_2 = 1;
  $output = array();
  while(count($output) < $count){
    if(count($output)==0){
      $output[] = $num_1;
    }
    else if(count($output)==1){
      $output[] = $num_2;
    }
    else {
      $new_number = $num_1 + $num_2;
      $output[] = $new_number;
      $num_1 = $num_2;
      $num_2 = $new_number;
    }
  }
  foreach($output as $num){
    echo $num. " ";
  }
}

When the function is invoked as generateFibonacci(5); the code displays
0 1 1 2 3 as the output.
Modify the function so that it returns (instead of displaying) the nth number (instead of
n numbers) in the Fibonacci series. For example, if you invoke the function as
generateFibonacci(5)it returns the 5th number in the series, i.e. 3. The modified
solution must also make use of a for loop instead of a while loop. The function must
only return a value if the number passed to it (in $count) is greater or equal to 1.
Otherwise, display an error message.

